# GENERATED FILE -- do not hand-edit. Consumed by `create_app(...; precompile_statements_file=...)`
# in the three .github/workflows/build_app_*.yml, and checked by src/build/check_statements.jl.
#
# Why this exists
# ---------------
# `precompile_execution_file="src/build/snoop.jl"` traces searches over fixtures small enough to
# ship. Real data compiles specialisations those fixtures never reach, and the shipped binary pays
# for them at startup. Measured on a 6-file Exploris search: a cold binary ran 291.53 s against
# 266.20 s for a warm package. After wiring this file in, the startup-attributable steps summed to
# +4.57 s.
#
# Harvested from TWO real searches, because one is not enough: a binary precompiled from one dataset
# and run on another re-JITs Pioneer methods that the first never exercised. Adding the second cut
# that from 152 to 47 on a third, independent dataset.
#
# What is NOT in here any more, and why that matters
# --------------------------------------------------
# This file used to carry ~56 statements for each (thread count, file count) pair, because
# `SearchContext{N,...}` was parameterised on the thread count and `ArrowTableReference{N}` on the
# number of input files. Both are user-supplied and unbounded, so no statements file could ever
# cover them -- a user on 8 threads with 4 files matched nothing we harvested. Those parameters were
# removed (see the notes in SearchTypes.jl), so the pipeline now specialises once instead of once per
# machine-and-experiment shape. Regenerate rather than hand-patch if you see ArrowTableReference{N}
# or SearchContext{<integer>, ...} reappear -- that means a parameter has crept back.
#
# PackageCompiler runs every line through Meta.parse -> Core.eval -> precompile and silently skips
# anything that throws, so a stale line degrades to a no-op rather than breaking the build. That
# makes staleness invisible, which is what src/build/check_statements.jl guards against.
#
# How to regenerate
# -----------------
#   1. Trace each real search. --pkgimages=no forces everything through the JIT so the trace is the
#      full set the run needs, not just what its pkgimage happened to miss.
#
#        julia --project=. --startup-file=no --pkgimages=no \
#              --trace-compile=trace_<name>.jl --threads 12 --gcthreads 8,1 \
#              -e 'using Pioneer; Pioneer.SearchDIA("<config>.json")'
#
#   2. For a complete regeneration, concatenate the traces, drop duplicates and any line that would
#      not survive PackageCompiler's pipeline, then prepend this header. For a focused code or
#      dependency change, retain the still-valid real-search corpus and add the new trace with:
#
#        julia --project=. src/build/refresh_precompile_statements.jl \
#              src/build/precompile_statements.jl /tmp/precompile_statements.jl trace_<name>.jl
#
#   3. Re-run src/build/check_statements.jl before committing. It should report 100%.
#
# Generated 2026-08-05 on Julia 1.12.5 from:
#   * a 6-file Olsen Exploris search, HYE library (384,515 precursors / 44,298 protein groups)
#   * a 3-file yeast search, trimmed 500-600 m/z library (17,444 precursors / 5,001 protein groups)
# Refreshed 2026-08-10 on Julia 1.12.6 for the portable-CPU dependency removal: 185 statements
# from the removed HostCPUFeatures/LoopVectorization/LinearSolve chain were pruned, and the changed
# target-neutral loops plus hand-written SIMD kernels were retraced with the deterministic Phase 1
# workload. The 5,581 surviving real-search statements were retained.
